{"ok":true,"data":{"kind":"command","command":"subject show","path":["subject","show"],"summary":"Show a subject (read-only)","effect":"read","effectNote":"refreshes the stale scenario-index cache once the subject is found; a refused call writes nothing","operands":[{"name":"id","valueName":"SUBJECT_ID","valueType":"string","required":true,"variadic":false,"default":null,"domain":{"pattern":"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$"},"help":"The subject to show"}],"options":[{"name":"repo","valueName":"DIR","valueType":"path","required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"defaultNote":"the nearest ancestor directory holding a canon.yaml","flagOnly":true,"help":"The repo to act on (default: the nearest ancestor directory holding a canon.yaml)"},{"name":"json","valueType":"switch","required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":false,"flagOnly":true,"help":"Output JSON instead of the human-readable form"},{"name":"as","valueName":"ROLE","valueType":"enum","possibleValues":["planner","implementer","reviewer","orchestrator"],"required":false,"repeatable":false,"default":null,"env":"CANON_ROLE","flagOnly":true,"help":"The role you act as: planner, implementer, reviewer or orchestrator. Overrides `CANON_ROLE`. `schema` and `context` list only the role's commands, `status` keeps its steps, and `--role` on `evidence add` / `evidence audit` / `review scenario` / `review change` is this role unless given"}],"errors":["CHANGE_ADOPTION_INCOMPLETE","CONFIG_REQUIRED","INTERNAL","REPO_UNREADABLE","ROLE_INVALID","SUBJECT_ADOPT_REFUSED","SUBJECT_NOT_FOUND","USAGE"],"outputs":[{"kind":"report","schemaRef":"#/schemas/SubjectShowReport","schemaVersion":"1.0"}],"examples":["canon subject show demo --json"],"schemas":{"Actor":{"description":"Who/what produced a record — structured, never a bare `by: String`\n(design D2, the donor audit's biggest cross-family gap).\n\n`role` is `Option` (S11 design D5, \"actor backfill is best-effort\nfrom adjacent fields; absent stays absent\"): a migrated legacy\nrecord whose only source field is a bare `by: \"legacy-ci-machine\"`\nstring carries no role information at all — `canon migrate` maps\nthat string to `agent_id` and leaves `role: null` rather than\nguessing, so the field must be able to express \"unknown\", not just\n\"known\". Every record canon itself originates still supplies a role\nvia [`Actor::new`]; only backfilled/migrated records use\n[`Actor::new_unattributed`].","properties":{"agent_id":{"type":"string"},"model":{"type":["string","null"]},"role":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/RoleId"},{"type":"null"}]},"session_id":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/SessionId"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["agent_id"],"type":"object"},"ChangeId":{"description":"openspec change slug: kebab-case (`[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*`), the directory name under `openspec/changes/` — joins: change ↔ tasks ↔ specs","type":"string"},"RecordKind":{"description":"The fourteen closed record kinds `canon-model` recognizes (design D1;\n`Subject` is the reviewed 13th kind, added by s36, and `Finding` the\nreviewed 14th, added by s43 — the \"a new kind is a reviewed, breaking\n`canon-model` change\" process design D1 mandates, exercised twice for\nreal). A fifteenth kind is again a reviewed, breaking\nchange — never a `kind: String` escape hatch (design D1's explicitly\nrejected alternative: an untyped `payload: serde_json::Value` would\nsilently recreate the \"no documented join key\" problem inside canon\nitself).","enum":["change","task","scenario","session","run","event","handoff","review","divergence","trajectory","strategy_item","evidence","subject","finding"],"type":"string"},"Reopen":{"description":"A recorded reopen of a shipped subject (see [`Subject::reopen`]).","properties":{"actor":{"$ref":"#/schemas/Actor","description":"Who reopened it."},"change":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/ChangeId"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The approved change the follow-up work goes into: the subject's\nnewest adopted change when it reopened. Absent when it adopted\nnone."},"reason":{"description":"The operator's reason, verbatim (one line).","type":"string"}},"required":["reason","actor"],"type":"object"},"RoleId":{"description":"kebab-case role slug (`[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*`), e.g. `implementer`, `reviewer` — joins: not a join-spine key; used by `Actor.role` and `regime_key`'s `<role>` segment","type":"string"},"SessionId":{"description":"opaque, non-empty agent-CLI session token; derivation source varies by adapter (Claude Code/Codex: transcript filename stem; omp/pi: in-file header `id` field) — this type validates shape only, never a single fixed format — joins: session ↔ cost ↔ run ↔ trajectory","type":"string"},"StatusOverride":{"description":"A recorded waiver of the `spec_coverage.require_review` status guard\n(see [`Subject::status_override`]). `canon gate check` reports a gap\nas an advisory naming this waiver only when it matches one of\n`waived` exactly, and only while the subject stays at `to`. A gap that\nappears later (a new blocker, a newly tagged scenario) is not covered\nand stays a violation.","properties":{"actor":{"$ref":"#/schemas/Actor","description":"Who waived it."},"reason":{"description":"The operator's reason, verbatim (one line).","type":"string"},"to":{"$ref":"#/schemas/SubjectStatus","description":"The status the transition moved to under this waiver."},"waived":{"description":"Exactly the guard violations this waiver let through, sorted.","items":{"$ref":"#/schemas/WaivedViolation"},"type":"array"}},"required":["to","reason","waived","actor"],"type":"object"},"StatusReason":{"description":"A recorded transition note (see [`Subject::status_reason`]).","properties":{"actor":{"$ref":"#/schemas/Actor","description":"Who gave it."},"reason":{"description":"The operator's reason, verbatim (one line).","type":"string"}},"required":["reason","actor"],"type":"object"},"Subject":{"description":"A subject (join-spine `subject_id` row: subject ↔ change ↔ scenario)\n— the durable product/management unit a team plans, designs, builds,\nand measures across many changes (s36, the reviewed 13th kind). A\nby-id kind like [`Change`]: flat Hive partition, no mandatory\n`scenario_id`. `domain` is a validated-shape-only kebab slug (see\n[`deserialize_domain_slug`] — the closed vocabulary lives in\n`canon/vocab`, not here); `owner_role` names the accountable role;\n`change_ids` accumulates as plan changes are adopted\n(additive-empty by default, so a freshly-authored subject with no\nlinks yet is still a valid, minimal record). One change may be listed\nby several subjects (0.18 D4); the change's own\n[`Change::subject_ids`] lists each of them, and readers join a\nsubject to its changes from both sides.\n\nThe scenario side of the join lives on [`Scenario::subject_id`], set\nby `canon inventory sync` from each scenario's `@subject:<id>` tag —\nthe spec corpus is the one place that link is authored. A subject\ncarries no copy of it: a second, separately-written list is exactly\nwhat drifted (never populated, so every reader saw zero scenarios and\nthe ship gate passed on an empty set). Records written before that\nlist was removed still deserialize; the stale key is ignored.","properties":{"actor":{"$ref":"#/schemas/Actor"},"at":{"format":"date-time","type":"string"},"change_ids":{"items":{"$ref":"#/schemas/ChangeId"},"type":"array"},"domain":{"type":"string"},"kind":{"$ref":"#/schemas/RecordKind"},"owner_role":{"$ref":"#/schemas/RoleId"},"reopen":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/Reopen"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Who reopened this subject from `shipped` to `verifying`, and why\n(0.18 D3, `canon subject move <id> --to verifying --reason`). Set\nonly on the record that reopens; every other `canon subject\nmove` write clears it, like [`Self::status_override`]. Skipped\nwhen absent, so every other subject stays byte-identical."},"schema":{"description":"Per-kind FORMAT GENERATION — the value\n[`RecordKind::schema_version`] defines and every writer stamps\nvia [`Envelope::current`] (design D2; `canon fmt`/`canon\nmigrate`, S11, key off it; `canon_store::fold::fold_latest_by_key`\norders an equal-`at` supersession tie by it,\n`s38-evidence-bearing-memory`). See\n[`RecordKind::schema_version`] for the bump rule — it is \"bump\nwhen two generations of one record can tie on `at`\", not \"bump on\nevery field addition\".","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"status":{"$ref":"#/schemas/SubjectStatus"},"status_override":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/StatusOverride"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The accountable waiver this record's status transition was let\nthrough under, when `spec_coverage.require_review` refused it and\nthe operator passed `canon subject move --override-reason`.\nSkipped when absent, so every subject written without one stays\nbyte-identical on the wire. Each `canon subject move` write\nclears it and sets it again only when it waives something, so a\nwaiver never outlives the status it was granted for."},"status_reason":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/schemas/StatusReason"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The note an operator gave the transition that wrote this record\n(`canon subject move <id> --to <state> --reason`, 0.21.1), on\nany transition; a reopen records it here too, next to\n[`Self::reopen`]. Every `canon subject move` write clears it\nand sets it again only when given a `--reason`. Skipped when\nabsent, so every other subject stays byte-identical."},"subject_id":{"$ref":"#/schemas/SubjectId"},"summary":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string"}},"required":["schema","kind","at","actor","subject_id","title","summary","domain","status","owner_role"],"type":"object"},"SubjectId":{"description":"subject slug: kebab-case (`[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*`), the durable product-unit identifier — joins: subject ↔ change ↔ scenario","type":"string"},"SubjectShowReport":{"$ref":"#/schemas/Subject","description":"`data` of the subject leaves: the Subject record, embedded verbatim (it keeps the ledger record's own schema and snake_case keys).","title":"SubjectReport"},"SubjectStatus":{"description":"A `Subject`'s lifecycle (s36 design D1): the states a product unit\nmoves through, `proposed → specced → building → verifying → shipped\n→ retired`. Transitions are policy-gated (CEL) at the CLI/gate layer\n(s35 seam); this enum owns only the closed set and its stable\nsnake_case wire spelling.","enum":["proposed","specced","building","verifying","shipped","retired"],"type":"string"},"WaivedViolation":{"description":"One violation a [`StatusOverride`] let through: the gate failure\nclass (`unreviewed-promotion`, `open-blocker`) and the violation's\nsubject (a scenario id, or `<change_id>#<round>.<seq>` for a\nblocker), as `canon gate check` prints them.","properties":{"class":{"type":"string"},"subject":{"type":"string"}},"required":["class","subject"],"type":"object"}},"x-canon":{"roles":["orchestrator"]}},"meta":{"command":"schema","schemaVersion":"1.2","tool":"canon","toolVersion":"0.35.0","contract":"atip/1","contractVersion":"1.2"}}
